# AWS Cloud Security Monitoring Lab

A hands-on AWS cloud security lab designed to help beginners understand and implement fundamental cloud security concepts using Terraform and native AWS security services.

---

## 🎯 Goal

The goal of this project is to build a small AWS security environment and understand how different cloud security controls work together.

The lab follows a practical, step-by-step approach where each AWS component is explained before it is deployed.

By following this repository, you will learn how to build, secure, monitor, and investigate a basic AWS environment using Infrastructure as Code.

---

## 🧠 Learning Objectives & Technologies

Through this lab, you will learn:

- AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)
- Principle of Least Privilege
- Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform
- EC2 security and basic hardening
- Security Groups and network access control
- S3 security and access control
- AWS CloudTrail logging
- Amazon GuardDuty threat detection
- Basic cloud security investigation
- Understanding security events and indicators
- Basic incident investigation and response

### Technologies & AWS Services Used

- Terraform
- AWS CLI
- AWS IAM
- Amazon EC2
- Amazon S3
- Security Groups
- AWS CloudTrail
- Amazon GuardDuty
- Linux

